WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.280
No matter what kind of stories you like, 2018
was a pretty great year for movies.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.740
The best ones served up scenes that took over
pop culture, becoming instantly iconic.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.820
These are the moments from our favorite movies
of the year that we'll still be talking about

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:14.820
for years to come.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.440
The Mission: Impossible series has become
a reliable adrenaline delivery system, and

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.680
2018's Fallout was no exception.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:27.100
The movie's setpieces are all impressive,
but the helicopter chase is the most breathtaking,

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.220
with Cruise actually learning to fly so he
could perform the scene's aerial maneuvers.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.740
Talk about raising the bar.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.040
"Not when I'm this close!

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:34.540
Come on!

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:35.040
Come on!"

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:47.300
A Star is Born is a classic showbiz fable,
and one of 2018's biggest hits.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:51.820
The scene in which Lady Gaga's Ally takes
the stage with Bradley Cooper's Jackson Maine

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.980
for the first time was instantly iconic.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.820
"Come sing that that song that I love.”

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:56.940
“No I can’t do that.”

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.260
“Wait.. that’s not funny."

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:04.160
The song, "Shallow," was a chart-topping sensation,
standing alone outside the context of the

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:04.660
film.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.020
But it makes for an incredible dramatic moment
in the movie's story too, one that's guaranteed

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.580
to linger in viewers' memories for years to
come.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:12.940
"Can I tell you a secret?

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:17.960
You might be a songwriter."

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.740
Bohemian Rhapsody could have ended with Freddie
Mercury's death, but instead, the story wrapped

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:28.120
up on a high point: Queen's legendary set
at 1985's Live Aid.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.400
Many consider the performance to be among
the best rock sets ever, which the bio-pic

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.400
faithfully recreated.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.340
"Thank you for making this a great occasion."

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.520
While only three songs made the movie's final
cut, the 20 minute, six song set was filmed

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.840
in its entirety, which fans will get to see
as an extra feature for the movie's home release.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:54.429
A Quiet Place was one of 2018's more unexpected
hits, a nail-biting sci-fi thriller from director

00:01:54.429 --> 00:01:59.060
John Krasinski, Nothing was a better testament
to his craftsmanship as a filmmaker than the

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:03.800
harrowing childbirth sequence, in which Emily
Blunt's character goes into labor while alien

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.500
beasts scour the house around her.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.640
Going into labor is a noisy experience, so
watching Blunt's character try and get through

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.300
it without making a sound was unbearably tense.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:23.920
It's the best sequence in the movie, and one
of the most memorable scenes of the year.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:29.620
Marvel's Black Panther was one of 2018's biggest
hits, filled with memorable locations and

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:30.960
magnetic performances.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.980
Everyone has their own favorite character,
but Danai Gurira's Okoye gets what's arguably

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:38.080
the movie's most crowd-pleasing sequence.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:42.469
In the movie's casino scene, Gurira steals
the show with an iconic moment that's both

00:02:42.469 --> 00:02:44.200
hilarious and badass.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:49.400
The scene starts with the heroes undercover,
with Okoye donning a wig to better blend in.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.500
She's not a fan of it.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:55.540
"Bast willing, this will go quickly and I
can get this ridiculous thing off my head."

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.640
"Looks nice — just whip it back and forth."

00:02:58.940 --> 00:02:59.480
"What?"

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.000
When the group's cover is blown, the warrior
wastes no time in whipping off her wig, and

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:04.620
weaponizing it.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.819
It's not often that an action scene can make
such a clear statement about beauty standards,

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.400
but Black Panther pulled it off with style
— literally.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:25.840
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse won over
audiences everywhere, bringing Marvel character

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.460
Miles Morales to the big screen for the first
time.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.790
Miles is a different kind of Spider-Man, full
of youthful exuberance and insecurity, which

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.220
his debut played up in winning fashion.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.860
“When do I know, that I’m Spider-Man?”

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.799
When Miles gets his powers, he isn't sure
if he's ready to take up the mantle of Spider-Man.

00:03:44.799 --> 00:03:48.920
After he receives guidance from other dimensions'
more experienced Spider-People, he learns

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:52.720
the lesson that he'll never be ready — he
just has to take a leap of faith.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:04:01.040
"What's Up Danger"
"What's Up Danger"

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.719
2018's most iconic scene came at the climax
of Avengers: Infinity War, and you already

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.100
know the one we're talking about.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.040
"You should've gone for the head."

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:22.079
The moment in which the Mad Titan Thanos accomplishes
his goal of snuffing out half of all life

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:26.699
was one of the most mindblowing sequences
the superhero genre has ever seen, instantly

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.900
becoming known simply as "The Snap."

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:33.940
Audiences watched in horror as Black Panther,
Doctor Strange, and more crumbled to dust,

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.380
ending the movie on a devastating cliffhanger.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.460
"I don't feel so good.”

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.700
“I don’t know what’s happening?”

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:45.960
“I don't wanna go."

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.840
It's a sequence that spawned a thousand memes,
endless speculation, and left fans wondering

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:53.440
how on Earth they could wait a year to see
the story conclude.

00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:58.120
The moment was a gamble, but it paid off big
time with an unforgettable scene that's unlike

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:01.080
anything that's come before it, comic book
movie or not.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:05.220
Audiences could have revolted — instead,
we're all waiting at the edge of our seats

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.560
to see how the story will end.

